From: Tensor G1 PRoot GPU experiment
Subject: [PATCH] wsialloc: open Android DMA heaps read-only

Android grants unprivileged applications read access to the public DMA heap
character devices. Allocation is performed by DMA_HEAP_IOCTL_ALLOC; the access
mode of the returned dma-buf is selected independently with fd_flags.

Opening the heap O_RDWR fails with EACCES in a rootless Termux/PRoot process
even though allocation from the heap is permitted. Match Android's
libdmabufheap and open the heap O_RDONLY.

---
 util/wsialloc/wsialloc_dma_buf_heaps.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/util/wsialloc/wsialloc_dma_buf_heaps.c b/util/wsialloc/wsialloc_dma_buf_heaps.c
index 5339166..f70a6fd 100644
--- a/util/wsialloc/wsialloc_dma_buf_heaps.c
+++ b/util/wsialloc/wsialloc_dma_buf_heaps.c
@@ -120,7 +120,10 @@ wsialloc_error wsialloc_new(wsialloc_allocator **allocator)
       return WSIALLOC_ERROR_NO_RESOURCE;
    }
 
-   dma_buf_heaps->memory_fd = open("/dev/dma_heap/" STR(WSIALLOC_MEMORY_HEAP_NAME), O_RDWR);
+   /* Android exposes dma-heap character devices read-only to apps. The heap
+    * handle only receives DMA_HEAP_IOCTL_ALLOC; access for the returned
+    * dma-buf is selected separately through heap_data.fd_flags above. */
+   dma_buf_heaps->memory_fd = open("/dev/dma_heap/" STR(WSIALLOC_MEMORY_HEAP_NAME), O_RDONLY | O_CLOEXEC);
    dma_buf_heaps->protected_fd = -1;
 
    if (dma_buf_heaps->memory_fd < 0)
